  <running_head>INSTITUTIONUM</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">§. Nam improbabile est species non</l>
    <l n="2">esse perpetuas. Ideo cum temporariæ</l>
    <l n="3">videantur speciæ à perpetuis discrepare,</l>
    <l n="4">nec tamen semper exiftunt, videri pos-</l>
    <l n="5">sent potius <i>ἀμαρτήματα τῆς φύσεως</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">adeoque monstra. Veruntamen hæc ratio</l>
    <l n="7">non est sufficiens. Nam nec rosæ sem-</l>
    <l n="8">per sunt. Itaque satis est, si sint rerum</l>
    <l n="9">determinatæ causæ, &amp; ipsæ determina-</l>
    <l n="10">ti effectus causa conditæ. Interim nihil</l>
    <l n="11">certi conclusum volo.</l>
    <l n="12" type="heading" level="2" para="true">III. Bonitas stellarum ex ipsarum</l>
    <l n="13" type="heading" level="2">sine &amp; effectu colligitur.</l>
    <l n="14" para="true">§. De illo actum est: de illis agetur.</l>
    <l n="15">Hoc tamen notari potest: præter illam</l>
    <l n="16">bonitatem generalem, qua ad Deum &amp;</l>
    <l n="17">homines referuntur, ipsis competere</l>
    <l n="18">aliam duplicem. Prima est, quod astra</l>
    <l n="19">tempora dispensent. Secunda, quod</l>
    <l n="20">inferiora omnia regant. Et de utraque</l>
    <l n="21">in posterioribus ad hoc agendum.</l>
    <l n="22" type="heading" level="2" para="true">IV. Perfectio astrorum maxima est</l>
    <l n="23" type="heading" level="2">inter omnia corpora, quoad actionis univ-</l>
    <l n="24" type="heading" level="2">ersalitatem &amp; gubernationem: licet for-</l>
    <l n="25" type="heading" level="2">te quoad perfectionem absolutam tanta</l>
    <l n="26" type="heading" level="2">non sit.</l>
    <l n="27" para="true">§. Magna inter Physicos est diff-</l>
    <l n="28">icultas: <i>An stellarum perfectio major sit</i>
    </l>
    <l n="29">
      <i>quam omnium corporum aliorum?</i> Ego</l>
    <l n="30">hanc quæstionem limitatione solven-</l>
    <l n="31">dam</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes />
</page>
